github.com:neovim/neovim.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/neovim/neovim.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/neovim/neovim","homepage":"https://neovim.io","size":355316,"stargazers_count":94890,"watchers_count":94890,"language":"Vim Script","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":6465,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":2020,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["api","c","lua","neovim","nvim","text-editor","vim"],"visibility":"public","forks":6465,"open_issues":2020,"watchers":94890,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"### Describe the bug\n\nfunctional/ui/cmdline_spec.lua fails on macOS Mojave, or gives warning on Linux.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nTEST_FILE=functional/ui/cmdline_spec.lua make test\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nTest succeeds without warnings.\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nOn Ubuntu-22.04, it gives the warning\r\n\"Screen changes were received after the expected state.\"\r\nfor the following two test:\r\n(1) cmdheight=0 with multigrid\r\n(2) cmdheight=0 can only be resized to 0 if set explicitly:\r\n\r\nOn macOS (Mojave), the test (1) fails as follows:\r\nExpected:\r\n |## grid 3\r\n  |*  /p^                       |\r\nActual:\r\n|## grid 3\r\n  |*  /p                       |\r\n\r\nThe reason for (1) is simple: since the option 'incsearch' is ON by default, after `feed '/p',` busy_start/stop events is sent to the screen and the cursor '^' is turned off/on.\r\nThis can be fixed by adding\r\n`    command('set noincsearch')`\r\nbefore the line 1247 in functional/ui/cmdline_spec.lua:\r\n`    feed '/p'`\r\nhttps://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/8fbe75b3dda7ab3b9e6df0d5406539bde4c80887/test/functional/ui/cmdline_spec.lua#L1247-L1248\r\n\r\nI don't know the origin of the problem in test (2), and not sure whether it is related with the issue https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/22154.\n\n### Neovim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.9.0-dev-877+g228684d2f-dirty\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nUbuntu-22.04, macOS (Mojave etc.)\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\ngnome-terminal, Terminal.app\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from repo","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/22155/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/22155/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/comments/1678773839","html_url":"https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/22154#issuecomment-1678773839","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/22154","id":1678773839,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAPphoM5kEA5P","user":{"login":"ghost","id":10137,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10137?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost","html_url":"https://github.com/ghost","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-08-15T11:20:38Z","updated_at":"2023-08-15T11:20:38Z","body":"The problem is in `update_screen`, it invalidates all `msg_grid` rows that are used for displaying a message, when the screen is scrolled down back https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/22d397c233b12a94ba36052d9e626ed61e25d488/src/nvim/drawscreen.c#L458-L468  \r\nBut then, if redraw type is `UPD_NOT_VALID`, `msg_grid` rows from 0 to `p_ch` are used for compositing in https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/22d397c233b12a94ba36052d9e626ed61e25d488/src/nvim/drawscreen.c#L535-L538  \r\nSo, any command that shows a scrolled message, and causes a `UPD_NOT_VALID` redraw should trigger the same bug. For example, `:split | echo \"\\n\"` command with `redrawdebug=invalid` set also triggers the bug.  \r\nHere's the fix I came up with:  \r\n```diff\r\ndiff --git a/src/nvim/drawscreen.c b/src/nvim/drawscreen.c\r\nindex 73dd584fb..608b7806d 100644\r\n--- a/src/nvim/drawscreen.c\r\n+++ b/src/nvim/drawscreen.c\r\n@@ -463,7 +463,7 @@ int update_screen(void)\r\n       // non-displayed part of msg_grid is considered invalid.\r\n       for (int i = 0; i < MIN(msg_scrollsize(), msg_grid.rows); i++) {\r\n         grid_clear_line(&msg_grid, msg_grid.line_offset[i],\r\n-                        msg_grid.cols, false);\r\n+                        msg_grid.cols, i < p_ch);\r\n       }\r\n     }\r\n     msg_grid.throttled = false;\r\n\r\n```","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/comments/1678773839/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"ghost","id":10137,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10137?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost","html_url":"https://github.com/ghost","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/comments/1681785443","html_url":"https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/22154#issuecomment-1681785443","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/22154","id":1681785443,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAPphoM5kPgJj","user":{"login":"Jun-T","id":7692465,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2OTI0NjU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7692465?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jun-T","html_url":"https://github.com/Jun-T","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jun-T/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jun-T/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jun-T/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jun-T/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jun-T/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jun-T/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jun-T/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jun-T/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jun-T/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-08-17T07:34:28Z","updated_at":"2023-08-17T07:34:28Z","body":"Thanks. The patch works for me.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"